# Repair Engine Rules

The repair engine is the technical moat. These invariants are non-negotiable.

## Prompt-level invariants

The system prompt MUST state:
- `objective_locked: true` — the model may not rewrite the objective.
- `approved nodes are immutable` — model must echo them verbatim in `preserve`.
- `human-edited args are protected` — model must not modify args on
  human-edited nodes; downstream regen must adapt around them.
- Response format is a single structured-output call matching the zod schema.
  No prose, no chain of thought, no alternate plans.

## Code-level invariants

- `repairIntent` opens a **fresh** AI SDK session per call. Do not thread
  conversation history.
- Response is validated with zod. On validation failure, throw — do not
  attempt to "fix" the model output silently.
- The function input shape MUST include the full dependency graph. Repair
  must not be asked to infer dependencies.
- Output shape: `{ replace: NewToolCall[], preserve: string[], remove: string[] }`.
- Locked node IDs MUST appear in `preserve`. If the model omits one, throw.

## Eval harness

- 9 fixture cases in `eval/fixtures/case-{01..09}.json`.
- Two modes: `EVAL_MODE=mock` (canned responses in `eval/mocks/`) and
  `EVAL_MODE=live` (real Claude).
- Live mode must hit 9/9 deterministically across 3 consecutive runs before
  Phase 3 starts. Track passing-run counts in `eval/.passing-runs`.
